AWS EFS (Elastic File System) Notes


What is EFS?

	Amazon Web Services EFS (Elastic File System) is a fully managed, scalable, cloud-based Network File System (NFS) service provided by AWS.

	It allows multiple EC2 instances to access the same shared file system simultaneously.

	Think of EFS like a shared storage drive in the cloud.



	Key Features of EFS
		Feature									Description
		
		Fully Managed		AWS handles servers, storage, scaling, and maintenance

		Elastic Scaling		Automatically grows and shrinks as files are added/removed
		Shared Storage		Multiple EC2 instances can mount the same filesystem

		Highly Available	Data is replicated across multiple Availability Zones

		Durable				Designed for high durability
		
		NFS Protocol		Uses NFSv4.1 / NFSv4.0
		
		Serverless 
		Compatible			Works with Lambda, ECS, EKS



