How EFS Works?

	Create EFS filesystem
	Create mount targets in VPC subnets
	Attach security groups
	Mount EFS on EC2 using NFS client
	Multiple servers can access the same files


EFS Use Cases

1. Shared Web Content

	Multiple web servers share the same files.

	Example:

		Apache/Nginx servers
		Shared uploads directory


2. Kubernetes Persistent Storage

	Used with:

		EKS
		Kubernetes Stateful applications


3. DevOps & CI/CD

	Shared artifacts/logs between:

	Jenkins agents
	Build servers



EFS Performance Modes

	1. General Purpose (Default)
		Low latency
	Best for:
		Web servers
		CMS
		Small applications


